out using the default center alignment, you don’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have to specify the alignment value, but you do need to add empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parentheses:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["BasicVStack() {","    \/\/ ...","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift compiler requires the parentheses in this case because of how the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"layout protocol implements this call site syntax. Specifically, the layout’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/callAsFunction(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" method looks for an initializer with exactly zero","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"input arguments when you omit the parentheses from the call site.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can enable the simpler call site for a layout that doesn’t have an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"implicit initializer of this type by explicitly defining one:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["init() {","    self.alignment = .center","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For information about Swift initializers, see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Initialization.html","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift Programming Language"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Interact with subviews through their proxies","type":"heading","anchor":"Interact-with-subviews-through-their-proxies"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To perform layout, you need information about all of its subviews, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the views that your container arranges. While your layout can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interact directly with its subviews, it can access a set of subview proxies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/Subviews","type":"reference"},{"text":" collection that each protocol method receives as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an input parameter. That type is an alias for the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubviews","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collection type, which in turn contains ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview","type":"reference"},{"text":" instances","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that are the subview proxies.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can get information about each subview from its proxy, like its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dimensions and spacing preferences. This enables","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you to measure subviews before you commit to placing them. You also","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assign a position to each subview by calling its proxy’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/place(at:anchor:proposal:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Call the method on each subview from within your implementation of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"layout’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/placeSubviews(in